This program initializes the BME280 sensor, reads the calibration data, and then enters a loop where it measures temperature, pressure, and humidity every second and prints the results to the console. It handles I2C bus errors and a sensor-absent condition by printing an error message and exiting the program.

Please note that the I2C bus is not automatically closed on every exit path in this program. You may need to add additional code to handle this depending on your specific requirements.

